      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mount_wilson_clark_county_nevada",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "For at least 10,000 years, the Southern Paiute have inhabited the Mount Wilson area, hunting and gathering in its springs and canyons.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mount_wilson_nevada",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mount Wilson is formed mainly from Jurassic Aztec Sandstone, whose cross‑bedded layers create the iconic red and white banded cliffs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mount_wilson_nevada",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Designated as wilderness in 2002, Mount Wilson protects southern Nevada's natural resources amid growing urban proximity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mount_wilson_nevada",
